questions.text:
An object of height 6 cm is placed at a distance of 30 cm from the optical centre of a concave lens of focal length 15 cm. Use the lens formula to determine:
(a) the distance of the image from the optical centre;
(b) the height of the image formed.

A mirror used for rear-view in an automobile has a focal length of 2.0 m. If a car is located 8.0 m from the mirror:
(a) find the position of the image of this car as seen in the mirror;
(b) draw the ray diagram for image formation by the rear-view mirror.
